@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Meet Ben";
}

<section class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Meet Ben</p>
    <h1>Technical depth, product judgment, and a bias toward useful work.</h1>
    <p>Ben Dewey is an independent product and technology leader based in Charleston, South Carolina. He is seeking his next leadership opportunity and is available for select advisory work.</p>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
    <h2>A career built by making complex work clearer.</h2>
    <p>Ben started as a hands-on application developer. That technical foundation grew into leading client projects and product, user experience, and delivery teams across enterprise and public-sector work.</p>
    <p>He has also helped grow consulting practices through sales and business development, connecting client needs with the right teams and shaping work through delivery. Most recently, he led large teams at EY. Technical books, open-source contributions, and conference talks reflect an earlier chapter of his career; founder work through Nuology remains part of his story.</p>
</section>

<figure class="process-image">
    <img src="~/images/product-strategy-whiteboard.webp" alt="Illustrative product workshop whiteboard with sticky notes moving from discovery through launch" width="1672" height="941" loading="lazy" />
    <figcaption>From discovery to launch, with feedback informing what comes next.</figcaption>
</figure>

<section class="content-section">
    <h2>How Ben works</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Start with the people, decisions, and outcomes that make the work matter.</li>
        <li>Connect product, design, technology, and delivery around a shared direction.</li>
        <li>Build momentum through clear priorities, honest communication, and practical iteration.</li>
    </ul>
</section>
